don website\nClose\nHome\nBack to home\nStudy\nSubjects\nFoundation Courses\nAI, Computer and Data Science\nBiological and Biomedical Sciences\nBusiness and Management\nChemical Sciences\nComparative Literature\nCreative Arts Media\nDentistry\nTheatre and Performance\nEarth and Marine Science\nEconomics and Finance\nEngineering\nEnglish\nEnvironmental Science\nFilm\nGeography\nGlobal Development\nGlobal and Public Health\nHistory\nLaw\nLiberal Arts\nLinguistics\nMaterials Science\nMathematics\nMedicine\nModern Languages and Cultures\nPhysics and Astronomy\nSociology, Politics and International Relations\nPsychology\nStudy at Queen Mary\nUndergraduate study\nPostgraduate study\nShort courses\nDegree Apprenticeships\nExperience Queen Mary\nOpen days\nInternational students\nLife on campus\nSchools and institutes\nAbout\nAbout home\nGiving\nWelcome\nHow to find us\nCalendar\nOur history\nAlumni\nFor East London\nGlobal\nFacts and figures\nFreedom of information\nWho's who\nSustainability\nArts and Culture\nThe Medical College of Saint Bartholomew\u2019s Hospital Trust\nEquality, Diversity and Inclusion\nVolunteering\nEducation and the student experience\nActive Curriculum for Excellence\nResearch\nResearch and Innovation\nResearch home\nStrategy, support and guidance\nResearch highways\nFeatured research\nFacilities and resources\nPublications\nPostgraduate research degrees\nNews\nResearch impact\nResearch culture\nResearch by faculties and centres\nHumanities and Social Sciences\nMedicine and Dentistry\nScience and Engineering\nCollaborations and partnerships\nCollaborate with us\nContact us\nPostgraduate\nPostgraduate\nSection home\nSection navigation\nTaught programmes\nWhy choose Queen Mary?\nTaught programme finder\nHow to apply\nAfter you apply\nKey dates and deadlines\nPostgraduate Tuition fees\nFunding a Masters\nUndergraduate to Postgraduate\nJanuary 2027 Start\nResearch degrees\nInternational Student Recruitment Flyers 2023-24\nWhy choose Queen Mary?\nApplying for a Research Degree\nFunding a PhD\nHow we support you\nGet in touch\nDeadlines\nAssociate Study\nOpen Events\nMasters events\nResearch events\nYour support network\nAccommodation\nFAQs\nQueen Mary University of London\nPostgraduate\nResearch degrees\nDeadlines\nKey Dates and Deadlines\nYou can apply online for all our Postgraduate Research programmes (doctorate or PhD). This page outlines the key dates and deadlines for both Home/ European and International students applying to Queen Mary University of London.\nMost PhD programmes at Queen Mary start in September-October or January each year. Enrolment at different points in the year may be possible, for example, where funding for a specific project starts mid-year. A small number of students start their programmes in late Spring (April/May).\nIf a non-standard start date is approved, please note that enrolment must be completed within two weeks of the programme start date.\nAcademic Technology Approval Scheme (ATAS)\nAny applicant who is not a European Economic Area or Swiss national, applying for a Postgraduate Research course, may require an Academic Technology Approval Scheme (ATAS) security certificate.\nIf you require an ATAS security certificate, you will need to obtain your ATAS certificate, before requesting a CAS. Queen Mary University of London will not issue a CAS until your ATAS certificate has been obtained. Applicants should note, during busy periods, it can take up to six weeks to receive your ATAS security certificate.\nDeadlines for funded studentships\nHumanities and Social Sciences Studentships: Wednesday 21 January 2026 (please check the advert for the project)\nLaw/CCLS studentships: Monday 4 December 2025 (5pm) (please check the advert for the project)\nSchool of Business and Management studentships: Friday 16 January 2026 (5pm)\nScience and Engineering Studentships: Wednesday 28th January 2026\nOther Science and Engineering Studentships: various (please check the advert for the project)\nMedicine and Dentistry studentships: various (please check the advert for project)\nChina Scholarship Council applicants for any subject area: Wednesday 28th January 2026\nDoctoral Training Partnerships: There may be an additional application and an earlier deadline. Please check the websites carefully.\nSeptember 2026 entry:\nOctober 2025 - Applicants for postgraduate research programmes for entry in September 2026 open\nThursday 25th December 2025 - Friday 2nd January 2026 - University Christmas Closure. (Online applications may be submitted during this period. We will endeavour to respond to applicant enquiries and process newly submitted applications as soon as possible upon reopening in January).\nMarch 2026 - Accommodation applications open. For further information, please visit our Accommodation pages.\nFurther information on Queen Mary Research Studentships can be found on our dedicated webpages.\nFooter navigation\nAccommodation\nAlumni\nSchools and Institutes\nCareers and Employability\nCollaborate with us\nContact\nEvents\nGlobal\nHow to find us\nInternational students\nJobs\nLibrary\nMyQMUL\nNew students\nNews\nOrder a prospectus\nOur brand\nParents\nProfessional services departments\nPublic Engagement\nQMplus\nStaff directory\nStaff intranet\nStrategy 2030\nStudents' Union\nTeachers\nTerm dates\nTrade Union Facility Time\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy and cookies\nSite map\nModern Slavery Statement\nSupplier fraud alert\nOFS Data\nContact the university\nQueen Mary University of London\nMile End Road\nLondon E1 4NS\n+44 (0) 20 7882 5555\nBack to top\nEdit this page", "links": [["honeypot link", "https://4xvmpmomo3.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/ProdStage"], ["Skip to main content", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/postgraduate/research/deadlines/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/postgraduate/research/deadlines/"], ["Study", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/postgraduate/research/deadlines/#primary-nav-study"], ["Close menu", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/